From: android-kitkat-tls12 <android-kitkat-tls12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/30] SNI tests on the ClientHello capture of b1fe85c

Tests first for SNI by default (the behaviour of conscrypt d745755,
b221fc9, 342097d, 966ae8a, f67d784). The capture helper of 0007cf6 /
b1fe85c now takes a ClientSocketMaker, so a test can make the client
socket in any way; upstream's wrapping client with
"localhost.localdomain" stays the default.

- createSocket(String host, ...) (both String constructors) sends SNI
  with that host; the test name is put into libcore's InetAddress cache,
  so no DNS is needed;
- an InetAddress socket, a "127.0.0.1" socket, a socket wrapped with an
  IPv4/IPv6 literal, and setHostname("127.0.0.1") send no SNI
  (RFC 6066 section 3);
- a wrapped socket with an IP-literal host leaves the peer InetAddress
  unresolved (no reverse DNS on the SNI path);
- jsse.enableSNIExtension=false sends no SNI, but an explicit
  setHostname() still does;
- setHostname() wins over the wrapped host; setHostname(null) turns SNI
  off.

Android 4.3 port (android-4.3_r3) of patch 0012 of the 4.4 series. The
same change; only line offsets differ.
